.TH CRS\-TUNNEL 1 "2026-06-12" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
crs\-tunnel \- manage ssh tunnels to the control room VNC sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crs\-tunnel
.IR open | close | status | connect
.RB [ \-\-session
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR H ]
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-ssh\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-site\-config
.IR FILE ]...
.RB [ \-\-viewer
.IR BIN ]
.RB [ \-\-view\-only ]
.RB [ \-\-password\-file
.IR PATTERN ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crs\-tunnel
opens, closes, probes, or attaches to ssh tunnels carrying the control
room VNC traffic.
Each session in
.B controlroom.yaml
maps a client-side
.I local_port
to
.I 5900+display
on its DAQ host, routed through the gateway with
.B ProxyJump
and authenticated with Kerberos (GSSAPI).
One master ssh per session keeps a control socket in
.BR ~/.crs/ ,
so tunnels survive (also the closing of the terminal they were opened
from) and can be probed
.RB ( "ssh \-O check" )
or closed
.RB ( "ssh \-O exit" )
without pkill.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B open
Open the tunnel(s).
Requires a valid Kerberos ticket
.RB ( "klist \-s" ).
.TP
.B close
Close the tunnel(s) via their control sockets and remove stale sockets.
.TP
.B status
Print one line per session: state, local port mapping, account.
Defaults to
.B \-\-all
when no target is given.
.TP
.B connect
Open the tunnel if needed, then launch a VNC client against the local
port. On macOS this runs
\fBopen vnc://localhost:\fIPORT\fR
(the built\-in Screen Sharing client); elsewhere it runs
.BR "vncviewer \-Shared" .
An explicit
.B \-\-viewer
overrides this on any platform.
Screen Sharing cannot be view\-only or read a password file, so on macOS
.B \-\-view\-only
or
.B \-\-password\-file
(or a site overlay with
.BR "view_only: true" )
uses a TigerVNC viewer instead, and stops with an error before launching
anything if none is found.
The viewer runs in its own session, so closing the terminal does not
close it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-session " NAME"
Operate on one named session.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " H"
Operate on every session on a host (short or FQDN).
.TP
.B \-\-all
Operate on every configured session.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Path to controlroom.yaml (default: ./config/, or
.BR CRS_CONFIG ).
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh\-config " FILE"
Alternate ssh config passed as
.BR "ssh \-F" ;
used by the test harness to alias cluster hosts to localhost.
.TP
.BI \-\-viewer " BIN"
VNC viewer binary for
.BR connect .
Overrides the macOS
.B open vnc://
default.
.TP
.BI \-\-site\-config " FILE"
Site overlay applied on top of controlroom.yaml; repeatable, in order.
Default: the
.RB : \-separated
list in
.BR CRS_SITE_CONFIG .
An overlay may set
.B personal_user
and
.B gateway
(last file wins),
.B view_only
(true in any file wins) and add
.BR sessions ,
which are never managed by
.BR crs\-remote (1).
Other keys, and names, local ports or host displays that repeat existing
ones, are errors. See
.BR remote\-site/README.md .
.TP
.B \-\-view\-only
.B connect
opens the viewer view\-only
.RB ( \-ViewOnly ).
Also on when a site overlay sets
.BR "view_only: true" .
.TP
.BI \-\-password\-file " PATTERN"
VNC password file passed to the viewer
.RB ( PasswordFile= ).
.B {account}
and
.B {session}
are replaced per session; if the file does not exist the viewer asks.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_SITE_CONFIG
Site overlays when no
.B \-\-site\-config
is given.
.TP
.BR CRS_CONFIG ", " CRS_GATEWAY
Base config path and gateway override (the gateway override beats overlays).
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
    crs\-tunnel open \-\-all
    crs\-tunnel status
    crs\-tunnel connect \-\-session dcs\-main
    crs\-tunnel close \-\-host mu2e\-mgr\-01
    crs\-tunnel connect \-\-site\-config remote\-site/sites/caltech.yaml \-\-session cr01
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.crs/ssh\-ctrl\-*
SSH control sockets, one per open tunnel.
.TP
.B ~/.crs/tunnels.log
Output of the tunnel ssh processes; errors are also shown by
.BR open .
.TP
.B ~/.crs/viewer\-*.log
Output of each viewer started by
.BR connect .
.TP
.B config/controlroom.yaml
Central session/gateway configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crs\-remote (1),
.BR crs\-gui (1),
.BR crs\-screen (1),
.BR ssh (1)
.SH REPOSITORY
.UR https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-controlroom-setup
https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-controlroom-setup
.UE
